    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Nuclear deterrence is the bedrock of global stability, as the threat of mutually assured destruction prevents outright, catastrophic war between major powers. The very existence of these weapons acts as a necessary guarantor of peace by raising the cost of aggression beyond any acceptable threshold. Without this ultimate deterrent, the world would inevitably descend into the brutal, large-scale conflicts that history has shown are far more devastating than any nuclear exchange.\n\nHere is a weak counter-argument for your student to dismantle:\nSome argue that nuclear weapons are inherently immoral because they carry the risk of mass death and indiscriminate destruction. They claim that relying on the threat of annihilation is a morally bankrupt way to maintain international order. This perspective often ignores the reality of geopolitical power dynamics and the current state of global conflict.",
